(:id "vt/c/generator-panic" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/ctable/vtcells_strict_test.go: TestCVariableCellsStrict, TestCVariableCellsStrictNegativeControl") :tested-revision "f3200f490a91da8b4cfd7f537066ff5924deaa1e" :note "2026-11-09: the fixed-form red is R2.schema's payload-free pong arm (v.F is nil; fixedCollectTypes used to panic) and A2.schema's direct string arm (the writer used to emit table_fixed_put0). TestCVariableCellsStrict generates both headers and the compiled probes require the pong arm to ignore boost residue and the string bytes to round-trip. TestCVariableCellsStrictNegativeControl plants the boost store into a copy of the pong case and a zero-length copy into the string arm; both probes fail at runtime, not by a compile error.")
(:id "vt/c/strict-read" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/ctable/vtcells_strict_test.go: TestCVariableCellsStrict, TestCVariableCellsStrictNegativeControl") :tested-revision "f3200f490a91da8b4cfd7f537066ff5924deaa1e" :note "2026-11-09: TestCVariableCellsStrict holds the generated C variable read to one strict result (whole value on a clean wire; whole refusal on a damaged, truncated, or out-of-range wire, and on a duplicate map key or a lone surrogate in JSON). TestCVariableCellsStrictNegativeControl turns off the out-of-range finish guard in a copy of the generated header and requires that compiled probe to fail.")
